abstract: >-
  A zero-Mathlib Lean 4.35.0 formalization of the Baker-Gill-Solovay oracle
  theorem in an explicit oracle Turing machine model, the counting step of the
  natural-proofs argument, and twelve classical supporting lemmas (14 statements
  C1-C14, accepted by six kernel checks with five checker implementations on
  Ubuntu CI). It also contains exact-arithmetic and SAT experiments, including
  three exact counterexamples and one numerical illustration against four
  illustrative SAT heuristics, and a 15-page white paper surveying twelve proposed
  pathways toward P vs. NP. All formalized results are known mathematics. P vs. NP
  remains open; no proof of P = NP or P != NP is claimed.
